  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 890 of the laws of 1982, relating to the establishment\nof certain water charges for hospitals and charities in New York city, in\nrelation to extending the effectiveness of such chapter for two additional\nyears",
    "basePrintNo": "S8071",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8071-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 890 of 1982",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8071\n\nSPONSOR: LANZA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 890 of the laws of 1982,\nrelating to the establishment of certain water charges for hospitals and\ncharities in New York city, in relation to extending the effectiveness\nof such chapter for two additional years\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation limits water charges for hospitals and charitable\norganizations.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends Chapter 890 of the Laws of 1982 to extend its expira-\ntion date until September 1, 2020. This legislation would continue\nreduced water rates for hospitals and charitable institutions in New\nYork City.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would extend for two years a long-standing reduction in\nwater charges offered to hospitals and other charitable organizations in\nNew York City. The continuation of the exemptions would help to ease\nsome of the financial burdens on these important institutions.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 273 of the Laws of 2016.\nChapter 246 of the Laws of 2014.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
